Description:

Cyrus now rejects RFC 5322 date-times containing non-ASCII bytes, such as in
a message's Date header, without reading outside its character tables.
Previously, such bytes caused out-of-bounds reads while parsing the date.

Reported by interpolwantme.  This is CYR-3527.


